-- title:
--   Cartan's vanishing criterion: Čech acyclicity on a stable class of objects implies vanishing of higher Ext from free sheaves
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal C$ be a site with topology $J$ and finite wide pullbacks, and let $F$ be a sheaf of abelian groups on $\mathcal C$, in a setting where sheaves of abelian groups have Ext groups and enough injectives. For $U\in\mathcal C$ write $\mathbb Z[U]$ for the free abelian sheaf on $U$ (the sheafification of the free abelian presheaf on the representable presheaf of $U$). For $f:V\to U$ write $\mathbb Z[V^{n+1}_U]$ for the free abelian sheaf on the $(n+1)$-fold fibre product $V\times_U\cdots\times_U V$, and $d_n : \mathbb Z[V^{n+2}_U]\to\mathbb Z[V^{n+1}_U]$ for the differentials of the Čech complex of free sheaves (alternating sums of face maps).
--
--   Let $P$ be a property of objects of $\mathcal C$. Assume that for every $U$ satisfying $P$ and every covering sieve $R\in J(U)$ there is a morphism $f:V\to U$ such that
--
--   1. the sieve generated by $f$ is a covering sieve of $U$;
--   2. every term $V^{n+1}_U$ of the Čech nerve of $f$ satisfies $P$;
--   3. Čech cocycles of $F$ in positive degrees are coboundaries: for every $m$ and every $\varphi:\mathbb Z[V^{m+2}_U]\to F$ with $\varphi\circ d_{m+1}=0$ there is $\psi:\mathbb Z[V^{m+1}_U]\to F$ with $\varphi=\psi\circ d_m$;
--   4. for every $q$ and every $\xi\in\operatorname{Ext}^{q+1}(\mathbb Z[U],F)$: if the pullback of $\xi$ along $\mathbb Z[g]$ vanishes for every $g:W\to U$ in $R$, then the pullback of $\xi$ along $\mathbb Z[f]$ vanishes.
--
--   Then for every $U$ satisfying $P$,
--   $$\operatorname{Ext}^{p+1}\big(\mathbb Z[U], F\big) = 0 \qquad\text{for all } p\ge 0.$$
--
--   Since $\operatorname{Ext}^{q}(\mathbb Z[U],F)$ computes the cohomology $H^q(U,F)$, this is a Cartan-type criterion deducing vanishing of higher sheaf cohomology on a class of objects from vanishing of Čech cohomology for suitable refining covers. Condition 4 holds for instance when $f$ refines a finite disjoint subcover contained in $R$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The site is `C : Type (u + 1)` with `Category.{u}` and `[HasFiniteWidePullbacks C]`; sheaves take values in `AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}`, with `[HasSheafify J _]`, `[J.HasSheafCompose (forget _)]`, `[J.WEqualsLocallyBijective _]`, `[HasExt.{w} (Sheaf J _)]` and `[EnoughInjectives (Sheaf J _)]`. Free sheaves are `freeAbelianSheafFunctor J`, the Čech terms and differentials are `cechFree J f n` and `cechFreeD J f n : cechFree J f (n+1) ⟶ cechFree J f n`, and pulling back an Ext class along $\mathbb Z[g]$ is `(Ext.mk₀ ((freeAbelianSheafFunctor J).map g)).comp ξ _`. The conclusion is stated as `ξ = 0` for all `ξ : Ext ((freeAbelianSheafFunctor J).obj U) F (p + 1)`.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014). Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Sites/SheafCohomology/Cartan.lean, lines 40-87 (`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.ext_free_eq_zero_of_cech`).

